eventually|finally|ADVERB|In the end|After some time, effort, or delay.|cuối cùng; rốt cuộc|After several attempts, the door eventually opened.|Sau vài lần thử, cuối cùng cửa cũng mở.|Not the same as possibly.|0
finish|complete|VERB|Complete an activity|To bring an activity to its end.|làm xong; kết thúc|Please finish the report before lunch.|Hãy làm xong báo cáo trước bữa trưa.|Finish noun or gerund.|0
finish|surface|NOUN|Surface treatment|The final surface appearance or coating of an object.|lớp hoàn thiện bề mặt|The table has a smooth satin finish.|Bàn có lớp hoàn thiện mịn, bóng nhẹ.|Countable; furniture context.|1
finish|ending|NOUN|End or finishing point|The end of an event or the point where a race ends.|kết thúc; đích|Spectators gathered near the finish of the race.|Khán giả tập trung gần đích cuộc đua.|Countable; race finish.|2
fixed|unchanging|ADJECTIVE|Not changing or moving|Set in place or established so that it does not change.|cố định|The ticket has a fixed price.|Vé có giá cố định.|Fixed position or amount.|0
formerly|previously|ADVERB|In the past|At an earlier time, before the present situation.|trước đây|The building was formerly a school.|Tòa nhà trước đây là một trường học.|Adverb of past status.|0
frighten|scare|VERB|Make afraid|To make someone feel afraid.|làm sợ hãi|The sudden noise frightened the puppy.|Tiếng động bất ngờ làm chó con sợ hãi.|Transitive; frightened person.|0
